---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import SpecTable from '../../../components/SpecTable.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import RequestResponse from '../../../components/RequestResponse.astro';
import GuardChain from '../../../components/GuardChain.astro';
import { url } from '../../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = 'Durable task lifecycle';
const pageDesc =
  'How long-running work survives a restart: the six states, the allowed transitions, idempotent submission, retry backoff, refusal codes and the 64 KiB bounds.';

const toc = [
  { id: 'why', title: 'Why a task queue' },
  { id: 'states', title: 'States and transitions' },
  { id: 'kinds', title: 'Task kinds' },
  { id: 'idempotency', title: 'Idempotent submission' },
  { id: 'retries', title: 'Attempts and backoff' },
  { id: 'bounds', title: 'Bounds and refusals' },
  { id: 'walkthrough', title: 'Walkthrough' },
];

const states = [
  { title: 'PENDING', detail: 'Accepted and stored. Any worker may claim it; nothing has run yet.', refusal: 'cancellable' },
  { title: 'RUNNING', detail: 'A worker holds the claim and is executing. The attempt counter has already been incremented.', refusal: 'running_not_cancellable' },
  { title: 'RETRY_WAIT', detail: 'The attempt failed in a way that is worth retrying. The backoff delay is counted down, and the job stays cancellable while it waits.', refusal: 'cancellable' },
  { title: 'SUCCEEDED', detail: 'The work finished and its result is stored with the row. Terminal.', refusal: 'not_cancellable' },
  { title: 'FAILED', detail: 'The attempt budget is spent, or the failure was not worth retrying. Terminal — unless the owner explicitly retries it.', refusal: 'retryable' },
  { title: 'CANCELLED', detail: 'The owner stopped it before it ran, or while it waited for a retry. Terminal.', refusal: 'not_cancellable' },
];

const transitions = [
  ['PENDING', 'RUNNING, CANCELLED', 'A worker claims it, or the owner stops it before the claim.'],
  ['RUNNING', 'SUCCEEDED, FAILED, CANCELLED, RETRY_WAIT', 'The one state with four exits: done, permanent failure, a cancelled-and-cooperative run, or another attempt later.'],
  ['RETRY_WAIT', 'PENDING, RUNNING, CANCELLED', 'The delay expires and the job is queued again, or the owner stops it while it waits.'],
  ['FAILED', 'PENDING', 'Only an explicit retry re-queues it, and only from FAILED.'],
  ['SUCCEEDED', '—', 'Terminal. Nothing transitions out.'],
  ['CANCELLED', '—', 'Terminal. Nothing transitions out.'],
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  path="/api/task-lifecycle/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: url('/') },
    { name: 'Reference', href: url('/api/') },
    { name: 'Task lifecycle', href: url('/api/task-lifecycle/') },
  ]}
  toc={toc}
  keywords={[
    'AutoTelegramForward durable tasks',
    'async task states Telegram',
    'idempotency key task API',
    'retry backoff dead letter',
  ]}
>
  <p>
    A session backup, a dead-letter replay, a whole-installation export: each of these outlives the HTTP request that
    starts it. Rather than holding a connection open, the API writes a row and returns it. The row is the contract —
    poll it, cancel it, retry it — and it is owned by the same tenant rule as everything else, which is why a foreign
    task id answers exactly like one that does not exist.
  </p>

  <Callout type="info" title="The 201/200 answer is the whole handshake">
    <p>
      <code>POST /api/tasks</code> returns the stored row, so a client does not have to follow up just to learn the id.
      The id, the state and the attempt budget all come back in the same response that accepted the work.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="why">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">Why a task queue instead of a long request</h2>
    <ul class="grid gap-2 list-none p-0 m-0">
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-[14.5px] text-slate-300">
        <span class="text-sky-400 font-bold shrink-0">·</span>
        <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Restarts do not lose work.</strong> The row is in the database, so a container replaced mid-backup comes back to a claimable PENDING job rather than an orphaned promise.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-[14.5px] text-slate-300">
        <span class="text-sky-400 font-bold shrink-0">·</span>
        <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Progress is observable.</strong> <code>GET /api/tasks</code> shows the state, the attempt count and the last error, so &quot;is it still running?&quot; is a query, not a guess.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-[14.5px] text-slate-300">
        <span class="text-sky-400 font-bold shrink-0">·</span>
        <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Failures are recoverable.</strong> A transient Telegram or network failure reaches RETRY_WAIT with backoff; a spent budget reaches FAILED, where an operator can retry it deliberately.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-[14.5px] text-slate-300">
        <span class="text-sky-400 font-bold shrink-0">·</span>
        <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Retries are safe.</strong> The idempotency rule means a client that retries a submission gets the original job back, not a second copy of the work.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="states">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">States and transitions</h2>
    <GuardChain steps={states} />
    <SpecTable
      class="mt-4"
      headers={['From', 'To', 'Trigger']}
      rows={transitions}
      caption="The complete transition table — anything not listed here is refused"
    />
    <Callout type="warning" class="mt-4" title="RUNNING is honest, not optimistic">
      <p>
        A cancel request against a RUNNING job answers <code>running_not_cancellable</code> rather than pretending to stop
        it. The worker only moves to CANCELLED if it observes the request cooperatively; otherwise the job finishes and
        lands on SUCCEEDED or FAILED. Reporting CANCELLED for a job that is still running would be a lie that a later poll
        would contradict.
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="kinds">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">Task kinds</h2>
    <SpecTable
      headers={['Kind', 'Started by', 'What it produces']}
      rows={[
        ['<code>session.backup</code>', '<code>POST /api/sessions/{id}/backup</code>', 'An encrypted archive of the session file, written only after the export succeeds.'],
        ['<code>dlq.replay</code>', 'Dead-letter replay from the dashboard or <code>POST /api/tasks</code>', 'The refused deliveries re-attempted against their original targets.'],
        ['<code>dlq.purge</code>', '<code>DELETE /api/dlq</code>', 'The caller\'s dead-letter entries removed, ownership applied before the delete.'],
        ['<code>backup.export</code>', '<code>POST /api/backup/export</code>', 'A configuration bundle that can be imported on another host.'],
      ]}
      caption="The kinds a caller may submit"
    />
    <Callout type="danger" class="mt-4" title="An unknown kind is refused, not guessed">
      <p>
        The kind must be one of the four above. Anything else answers <code>400 unknown_task_kind</code> — the queue
        dispatches on a closed set, so a typo cannot silently queue work that nothing will ever run.
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="idempotency">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">Idempotent submission</h2>
    <p class="m-0 mb-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      The identity of a job is the trio of <strong class="text-slate-100">owner</strong>,{' '}
      <strong class="text-slate-100">kind</strong> and <strong class="text-slate-100">idempotency_key</strong>. The owner
      comes from the verified token — never from the body — so two tenants may use the same key without colliding, and a
      client that retried a submission after a timeout gets its original job back instead of duplicating the work.
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <CodeBlock
        label="First submission — 201 Created"
        language="json"
        content={`{
  "task": {
    "id": "6f1c…",
    "kind": "dlq.replay",
    "status": "PENDING",
    "idempotency_key": "replay-2026-10-19",
    "attempt": 0,
    "max_attempts": 3
  },
  "already_existed": false,
  "id": "6f1c…",
  "status": "PENDING"
}`}
      />
      <CodeBlock
        label="The same submission again — 200 OK, same job"
        language="json"
        content={`{
  "task": { "id": "6f1c…", "status": "RUNNING", "attempt": 1 },
  "already_existed": true,
  "id": "6f1c…",
  "status": "RUNNING"
}`}
      />
    </div>
    <Callout type="tip" class="mt-4" title="Choose a key that describes the work, not the attempt">
      <p>
        A key derived from the intent — the day, the batch, the rule — makes a retry safe. A random key makes every retry
        a new job, which is exactly the behaviour idempotency keys exist to prevent.
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="retries">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">Attempts and backoff</h2>
    <SpecTable
      headers={['Rule', 'Value', 'Why']}
      rows={[
        ['Default attempt budget', '<code>3</code> attempts', 'Enough to ride out a transient failure, short enough that a permanent one is reported the same day.'],
        ['Maximum attempt budget', '<code>8</code>', 'A requested budget is clamped server-side rather than rejected, so an exaggerated value cannot create an unbounded retry loop.'],
        ['Backoff', '<code>5s → 20s → 80s → …</code>, factor 4, capped at <code>5 min</code>', 'Growth fast enough to stop hammering a service that is down, capped so a long queue still drains.'],
        ['Attempt accounting', 'Incremented when the attempt starts', 'A worker that dies mid-attempt does not get a free retry; the attempt it was running is visible in the row.'],
        ['Explicit retry', 'FAILED → PENDING with a fresh budget', 'An operator who fixed the cause re-queues the job; anything not in FAILED answers <code>not_retryable</code>.'],
        ['Terminal retention', '30 days by default, configurable', 'Finished rows are purged by a scheduled job; nothing that is still PENDING, RUNNING or RETRY_WAIT is ever eligible.'],
      ]}
      caption="Retry behaviour, in the order you will meet it"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="bounds">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">Bounds and refusals</h2>
    <SpecTable
      headers={['Condition', 'Answer', 'Detail']}
      rows={[
        ['Payload or result over the cap', '<code>400</code> <code>payload_too_large</code>', 'Each is capped at <strong>64 KiB</strong> and must be valid JSON. The message names which side exceeded the cap.'],
        ['Unknown kind', '<code>400</code> <code>unknown_task_kind</code>', 'The dispatcher works on a closed set of four kinds.'],
        ['Cancelling a finished job', '<code>400</code> <code>not_cancellable</code>', 'A SUCCEEDED, FAILED or CANCELLED job can only be retried (if FAILED) or ignored.'],
        ['Cancelling a running job', '<code>400</code> <code>running_not_cancellable</code>', 'The row is left in RUNNING, because that is the truth.'],
        ['Retrying anything not FAILED', '<code>400</code> <code>not_retryable</code>', 'Only a failed job has an attempt budget left to spend.'],
        ['Reading or cancelling a foreign job', '<code>404</code> <code>not_found</code>', 'Owner and id are both in the query, so the answer is the same as for a job that never existed.'],
        ['Listing without bounds', '<code>GET /api/tasks</code>', 'Pages with <code>limit</code> (1–200, default 50) and <code>offset</code>; an out-of-range value is clamped before it is narrowed to an int.'],
      ]}
      caption="Every way a task call can be refused"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="not-prose scroll-mt-24" id="walkthrough">
    <h2 class="display-3 text-white mb-3 scroll-mt-24">Walkthrough</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-4">
      <RequestResponse
        exchange={{
          label: 'Submit, poll, then recover a failed job',
          note: 'The same key is used for both submissions, so the second call is answered from the store. Only after the job reaches FAILED does the explicit retry become legal.',
          status: '201 → 200 → 200 OK',
          request: `# 1 — submit (retry-safe)
POST /api/tasks
{
  "kind": "dlq.replay",
  "payload": { "ids": ["a1","a2"] },
  "idempotency_key": "replay-2026-10-19",
  "max_attempts": 3
}

# 2 — poll one job
GET /api/tasks/6f1c…

# 3 — it exhausted its attempts
GET /api/tasks/6f1c…
{ "task": { "status": "FAILED", "attempt": 3, "max_attempts": 3 } }

# 4 — retry it, now that the cause is fixed
POST /api/tasks/6f1c…/retry`,
          response: `{
  "task": {
    "id": "6f1c…",
    "owner_user_id": 5094837833,
    "kind": "dlq.replay",
    "status": "PENDING",
    "attempt": 0,
    "max_attempts": 3,
    "created_at": 1790000000
  },
  "already_existed": false,
  "id": "6f1c…",
  "status": "PENDING"
}`,
          requestLanguage: 'text',
        }}
      />

      <RequestResponse
        exchange={{
          label: 'A cancel that is refused, honestly',
          note: 'A reminder that the API reports state rather than intent: the row is not silently marked CANCELLED, so a poll series never shows a value the worker contradicts.',
          status: '400 Bad Request',
          tone: 'err',
          request: `POST /api/tasks/6f1c…/cancel`,
          response: `{
  "error": "running_not_cancellable",
  "error_code": "running_not_cancellable"
}`,
          requestLanguage: 'text',
        }}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
